{"title":"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Each of its side lengths is multiplied by the same positive integer to produce a new square. Which of the following could be the area of the new square?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/34113adb7c5c0d3ec17607e157782170fd63b61f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 70 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 80 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 90 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each side length is multiplied by a positive integer, the area must be multiplied by a perfect square. We can divide each answer choice by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> until we get a result that is a perfect square:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd0c67a285260faaba07cd52c5928a046d17680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60}{10} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a2fc1e742d17815a58b3712adb42546da2cdd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{70}{10} = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/6/3c67e27c10e9019440fab8e9ed6ca9f34359a4ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{80}{10} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb2424634d69ac532a11937076fb231d91d9fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{90}{10} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />. This is a perfect square, so the new area can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886ef4d560abe7503997803db619789cd37ea39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1\">Solution 1.1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since each side length is multiplied by a positive integer, the area must be multiplied by a perfect square. We can multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> by different perfect squares until we get one of the answer choices:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22be2e884065076706eacd92d3209bec7337b583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 1^{2} = 10 \\times 1 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80c2b257e58e9ec482884ffabf8856724544827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 2^{2} = 10 \\times 4 = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b61dac78c2e59edb4f06e907f1e972b55c4c8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\times 3^{2} = 10 \\times 9 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"222\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat\">2026 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Pr